# Sonora ships with no dependencies; playwright is installed only to run the
# browser tests in tools/, and none of that belongs in the repository.
# Both spellings. The trailing slash matches a directory and nothing else, so
# a `node_modules` *symlink* — which is how you point this checkout at a
# playwright installed somewhere else — sailed straight past it and got
# committed, carrying an absolute path that means nothing on another machine.
node_modules
node_modules/
package.json
package-lock.json

# Test artefacts.
#
# `shots/` and `shots-layout/` are reports — a picture of each step or each
# width, useful to look at after a run and meaningless afterwards.
#
# `shots-looks/` is different and is *not* ignored: it is the accepted
# appearance, the thing `tools/looks.mjs` compares against, and a regression
# test whose truth exists only on the machine that last ran it cannot catch a
# regression on anybody else's checkout (J4). Its `_diff/` subdirectory is per
# run — what the app looks like *now* when something disagrees — and that part
# stays ignored.
shots-*/
shots/
# Re-included: git will not look inside a directory it has excluded, so the
# directory itself has to be un-excluded before its contents are considered.
!shots-looks/
shots-looks/_diff/

# Python bytecode. `make-testlib.py` is a script rather than a module, but
# importing it to build a fixture library makes CPython write one of these
# beside it — and one got committed that way.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Windows shell metadata
desktop.ini
Thumbs.db
